  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The most appropriate way to allow an on-premises Ubuntu server to communicate securely with AWS CodeDeploy is to <b>include the IAM user credentials in the CodeDeploy configuration file, install the CodeDeploy agent, and let it register the server automatically</b>. This approach follows AWS CodeDeploy's recommended best practices for registering on-premises instances. <br/><br/>The option <i>Assign an IAM role to the on-premises machine with the necessary CodeDeploy permissions and utilize the register command of the AWS CLI to associate the role with the server</i> is not feasible because IAM roles cannot be assigned directly to on-premises servers—only to AWS services and resources. <br/><br/>The option <i>Use the AWS CLI register-deploy command to create an IAM user for the server, store the user's credentials in the server’s configuration, and then register the server with CodeDeploy</i> is incorrect since there is no 'register-deploy' command, and the registration process depends on the CodeDeploy agent and proper configuration files. <br/><br/>The option <i>Run the AWS CLI tag-resource command to set up an IAM user for the on-premises server, register it with CodeDeploy, and assign a tag so that CodeDeploy can manage deployments to it based on the tag</i> is also inaccurate because tagging resources is for organizing and filtering, not for registration and authentication.<br/><br/><b>Tip:</b> Always ensure IAM credentials are managed securely, and follow AWS documentation for properly installing and registering the CodeDeploy agent for on-premises deployments.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your organization maintains a legacy Ubuntu server in its on-premises data center that hosts several critical applications. The business goal is to leverage AWS CodeDeploy to streamline deployment of new application updates to this particular on-premises instance. Before doing so, the server needs to be registered with CodeDeploy using IAM user credentials for secure authentication. <br/>Which approach should you take to best achieve this setup?</p>",
